<article>
	<h1><span>Storefront: SKU</span></h1>

	<ul class="nav">
		<li><a href="#overview">Overview</a></li>
		<li><a href="#fields">Fields</a></li>
		<li><a href="#toolbar">Toolbar</a></li>
	</ul>

	<section id="overview">
		<h2><span>Overview</span></h2>

		<p>This is where you can add a new SKU to a product or edit an existing SKU. Some fields only appear for
			certain product types, as noted below.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="fields">
		<h2><span>Fields</span></h2>

		<h3>Details</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Title</dt>
			<dd>The name of the SKU. Required.</dd>

			<dt>Price</dt>
			<dd>The price of the SKU. Required.</dd>

			<dt>Weight</dt>
			<dd>The weight of the SKU. Only shown for products of the Shippable merchandise type.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Checkout options</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Checkout notes/comments message</dt>
			<dd>A text field.</dd>

			<dt>Checkout notes/comments required</dt>
			<dd>A choice of No or Yes.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Product options</h3>
		<p>Only shown when the product has option groups.</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>One field per option group</dt>
			<dd>A drop-down list, labeled with the name of the option group, to pick the option this SKU has.
				Required. It lists the published options of the group, and any option the SKU already has. If the
				group has no such options, a warning with a link to the group's options is shown instead.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>General Software-related Options</h3>
		<p>Only shown for products of the Software Download type.</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>EULA (overrides product-level EULA)</dt>
			<dd>The text of the end-user license agreement for this SKU, entered in a text editor.</dd>

			<dt>Download file</dt>
			<dd>A text field. Required.</dd>

			<dt>Total Downloads Limit</dt>
			<dd>A text field.</dd>

			<dt>Downloads Limit per Single User</dt>
			<dd>A text field.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Serial numbers</h3>
		<p>Only shown for products of the Software Download type.</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Serial Number Management</dt>
			<dd>No management, Single Universal Number or Multiple Unique Numbers. When the saved choice is
				Multiple Unique Numbers, a <strong>Manage multiple serial numbers</strong> link appears below,
				which opens the list of the SKU's serial numbers.</dd>

			<dt>Single Serial Number</dt>
			<dd>A text field, used with the Single Universal Number choice.</dd>
		</dl>

		<p>The right-hand column shows:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>ID</dt>
			<dd>The identification number of the SKU, assigned by the system. It cannot be changed.</dd>

			<dt>Product</dt>
			<dd>The name of the product the SKU belongs to.</dd>

			<dt>Downloaded</dt>
			<dd>How many times the SKU has been downloaded. Only shown for products of the Software Download
				type.</dd>

			<dt>Direct URL</dt>
			<dd>The address of the product in the storefront, followed by the IDs of the SKU's options, if it has
				any.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Options</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Allow multiple</dt>
			<dd>A choice of No or Yes.</dd>

			<dt>Track Inventory</dt>
			<dd>Whether the inventory level is kept track of. If Yes, set the Inventory field.</dd>

			<dt>Inventory</dt>
			<dd>The number of items available for sale. A whole number, zero or more.</dd>

			<dt>Inventory notification threshold</dt>
			<dd>When the inventory is at or below this number, an email is sent to the admin on each inventory
				change.</dd>
		</dl>
		<p>Track Inventory and Inventory are not shown for a Software Download SKU that uses Multiple Unique
			Numbers.</p>

		<h3>Publishing options</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>State</dt>
			<dd>Unpublished or Published.</dd>

			<dt>Publish up</dt>
			<dd>A date and time, chosen with a calendar.</dd>

			<dt>Publish down</dt>
			<dd>A date and time, chosen with a calendar.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Restrictions</h3>
		<dl>
			<dt>Restrict by users</dt>
			<dd>A choice of No or Yes. When the saved choice is Yes, a <strong>Manage restrictions</strong> link
				appears below, which opens the list of the SKU's restrictions.</dd>
		</dl>

		<h3>Whitelist</h3>
		<p>Whitelisting grants users access to the SKU despite any other existing access controls or restrictions.
			The <strong>Manage whitelist</strong> link opens the SKU's whitelist.</p>
	</section>
	<section id="toolbar">
		<h2><span>Toolbar</span></h2>
		<p>At the top right you will see the toolbar.</p>
		<p>The functions are:</p>
		<dl>
			<dt>Save</dt>
			<dd>Saves the SKU and stays on this screen.</dd>

			<dt>Save &amp; Close</dt>
			<dd>Saves the SKU and returns to the list of SKUs of its product.</dd>

			<dt>Cancel</dt>
			<dd>Discards any changes and returns to the list of SKUs of its product.</dd>

			<dt>Help</dt>
			<dd>Opens this help screen.</dd>
		</dl>
		<p>Save and Save &amp; Close only appear if you may edit products.</p>
	</section>
</article>
